WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
We have a lot of choices
to make about our diet.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.480
Add to that, doing
the right thing

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:07.620
when it comes
to preventing

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.940
and treating a
chronic disease,

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.280
fighting a virus,
or losing weight,

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.740
and suddenly our
nutrition choices

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.140
can seem almost
overwhelming.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.480
Well, I’m here to help.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.700
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.471
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.040
Today we take a look
at the best way

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.900
to take care of
the largest organ

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.260
in our body: our skin.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.860
In our first story, almonds
are put to the test

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.300
in a randomized
controlled trial

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.463
for facial wrinkles.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.960
After my video on dates
blew my mind, showing that

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.360
eating just a few dates
can significantly reduce

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.520
the duration of labor
during childbirth and

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.369
improve the
progression of labor.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.580
But there are some surprising
benefits attributed to nuts

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.400
in randomized controlled
trials, like how about a study

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.040
on the effects of almond
consumption on wrinkles?

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.620
Where’d they even
come up with the idea?

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.860
Well, population studies
have found that healthy diets

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.840
are associated with
less facial wrinkles,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.720
like a meat and junk-
predominant eating pattern

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.000
was associated with
more wrinkles, whereas

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.940
a fruit-predominant pattern was
associated with fewer wrinkles.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.660
In terms of single foods,
yellow vegetables and soy

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.780
appear protective, but
wine may make things worse.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.120
Their thinking is that it
might be the antioxidants

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.820
in healthy foods decreasing
the oxidative stress load,

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:30.960
or the anti-inflammatory benefits,
or protection from sun damage,

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.140
or improved collagen production,
or better DNA repair.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.080
I have videos on most
of those topics.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.820
The bottom line is
that eating healthier

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.300
may reduce wrinkling, which
could actually save lives

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.280
if people started eating healthier

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.980
to maintain a more youthful
appearance and get all

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.560
the chronic disease benefits
as a happy side effect.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:53.820
Other studies have found the same
thing, supporting recommendations

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.240
for more healthy foods like
fruits, vegetables, and nuts.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.220
Here’s another
study that landed on

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.500
yellow vegetables,
and greens as well.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.860
In this study, a high intake of
vegetables, beans, and olive oil

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.180
appeared to be protective against

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.280
spots of precancerous
sun damage,

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.520
whereas a high intake of meat
and dairy may make things worse.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:15.840
Prunes, apples, and tea
seemed particularly good,

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.300
but this was a
cross-sectional study,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.280
meaning just a snapshot in time.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.220
Maybe people who eat more meat
are out barbequing in the sun,

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:27.540
or people who eat more prunes
just use more sunblock.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.240
You can’t know for sure if
foods actually affect wrinkling

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.300
until you... put them to the test—

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:38.160
but we had no such
studies…until, now.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.280
Why study almonds?

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.400
Because it was paid for by
the Almond Board, of course.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.180
The researchers didn’t know
who was in the nut group, though,

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.500
and who was in
the control group,

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.360
until they were
looking at the results.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.960
The nut group were given
2 ounces of nuts a day,

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:57.960
like two palmfuls of nuts, and
the control group was instead

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.000
given nut-free snacks
to eat instead

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.400
like nut-free granola
bars or pretzels.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.900
Before and after, they got
high‐res facial photographs

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:11.040
to quantify facial wrinkle
depth and severity using

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.420
a computer‐based photographic
analysis and…boom,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.960
the almond group had significantly
decreased wrinkle severity

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:24.060
compared with the control group
by the end of the 16-week study.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.340
The paper concludes:
“Our study demonstrates that

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:29.340
daily almond consumption
may reduce wrinkle severity...”

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.420
Now, they used a relatively
large dose, 2 ounces a day,

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:35.820
whereas you can get
cardioprotective benefits

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.220
of nuts from even less
than a half an ounce;

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.460
so, who knows, maybe they could
have gotten away with using less.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:44.400
Here’s the low-dose nut
study they referenced,

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.940
showing a significant drop in
LDL cholesterol within 6 weeks

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.430
eating just a few
almonds a day—10 grams

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.380
which is just like
8 almonds a day.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.200
That’s the nice thing
about healthy foods,

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.240
they just have good
side effects.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:00.660
So, global disease prevention
strategies might beneﬁt

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:04.080
from emphasizing that a
healthy diet is also linked

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:07.860
to less facial wrinkling,
and maybe vanity will help us

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:11.473
prevent a few heart
attacks in the bargain.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:12.720
In our next story,

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:14.160
we discover how
some foods

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.120
appear protective

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.860
against the development
of skin wrinkles—

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:20.171
while others may
make them worse.

00:04:20.516 --> 00:04:24.120
The skin is the largest
organ in the body—

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.380
about 20 square feet—

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.140
and, the most vulnerable
organ in the body,

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.260
exposed to both the oxidizing effects
of UV radiation from the sun,

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:34.980
and the oxidizing effects
of oxygen in the air.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:38.640
And, years of oxidant
stress can take a toll.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:41.100
Over the years, skin becomes
thinner, more easily damaged;

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.400
loses volume, elasticity,
and can sag and wrinkle.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.140
What can we do about it?

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.440
“Skin wrinkling: can
food made a difference?”

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:56.220
They measured healthfulness of skin
using a microtopographic method.

00:04:56.220 --> 00:05:00.900
It’s cool; they make a mold of the back
of your hand with a silicone rubber,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.660
peel it off, and then look at it
under a microscope.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:04.800
This is what young, tight,
healthy skin looks like.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.400
But, then, as we age, our skin
can get all coarse and flaccid.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.080
How can we stop it?

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.080
Well, three things contribute
to the aging of skin:

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.020
“Oxidative stress…induced by
[sun]-damage, inflammation

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:18.660
and ischemia [lack of
adequate blood flow].”

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.380
Oxidative stress means
we need antioxidants.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.340
“Under these circumstances, many
skin antioxidants undergo depletion…

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:31.620
and must be replaced continuously
in order to delay the otherwise inevitable

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:34.140
deterioration which would
lead to skin aging.”

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.900
So, plant foods would
presumably help.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.720
And then, inflammation
and lack of blood flow.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:43.260
And so, one might predict that
saturated fat (inflammation)

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:44.580
and cholesterol (ischemia),

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:47.520
might be associated with
adverse effects on our skin.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:50.160
Let’s see if our predictions hold up.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.020
“In particular, a high intake
of vegetables, [beans, peas, lentils, soy]

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:58.140
and olive oil appeared to be
protective” against skin wrinkling,

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:00.300
whereas “a high intake
of meat, dairy and butter”

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.280
appeared to have an adverse effect.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.300
Prunes, apples, and tea
appeared especially protective.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:11.040
A recent study, for example,
found that green tea phytonutrients

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:14.280
were able to protect skin
against harmful UV radiation,

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:17.280
and help improve skin quality of women.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.440
After a few months on green tea,

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.320
there was a 16% reduction
in skin roughness,

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:23.188
and a 25% reduction in scaling.

00:06:23.188 --> 00:06:25.020
Here’s micrographs showing
the reduction in scaling,

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:29.489
as well as improved skin
elasticity and hydration.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.560
Finally today, we
ask the question:

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.920
instead of treating
sensitive skin topically,

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.120
with lotions and creams,

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.040
why not treat it from
the inside out—

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.402
with diet?

00:06:40.665 --> 00:06:46.080
About half of the American population
says they have sensitive skin,

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:49.680
defined loosely as
“tingling, chafing, burning,”

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.500
itching sensations when exposed
to various environmental factors.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:55.080
A similar high prevalence
has been reported

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.660
throughout Japan and Europe—
especially in women.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:03.720
Often, there are no obvious signs,
and, so, it’s often been dismissed by

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:07.200
the medical community as a
“princess and the pea” phenomenon—

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.740
a mindset that has hindered
the investigation of this problem.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.080
But, now, it’s largely

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:17.040
“recognized as a genuine phenomenon
of physiological origin,”

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.260
thought to
arise from an

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:23.100
“alteration of the skin barrier allowing
potentially irritating substances

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:26.280
to penetrate the skin and generate
an inflammatory reaction.”

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.980
Okay, so, what can
we do about it?

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:35.100
Well, recently, supplementation
of flaxseed oil was found to diminish

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:38.580
skin sensitivity and improve
skin barrier function and condition.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:42.780
In a randomized, double-blind,
12-week study,

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:46.800
women were given about a half
teaspoon of flaxseed oil a day—

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:50.400
internally—versus safflower oil,
as a control.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:55.260
That’s the amount of oil found in about
a teaspoon and a half of flaxseeds.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:08:00.900
After three months, there was a
significant decrease in skin reddening

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:03.660
in the flax group compared
to the safflower group,

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:06.480
when an irritant chemical
was painted on their forearms

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:07.740
to measure skin sensitivity.

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:11.160
Their skin also ended up
significantly better hydrated,

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.440
had significantly better
barrier function—

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:18.000
as evidenced by lower
transepidermal water loss—

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:23.040
skin that’s less rough;
less scaly; and smoother.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:27.240
You can actually see the changes
in a close-up view of the skin.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:31.140
Skin looked pretty much
just as dry and scaly

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:33.300
before and after the
safflower oil intervention,

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:36.480
but significantly improved
after flaxseed oil.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:42.540
Sensitive skin is typically treated by
topical application of lotion and creams.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.600
But, why not treat it
from the inside?

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:49.620
“This study showed that daily
supplementation with flaxseed oil

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:53.040
improved skin appearance and
led to a decreased skin sensitivity

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:57.840
by improving epidermal barrier function
and decreasing inflammation…”

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:04.140
The best source of flax seed oil
is within the flaxseed itself, right?

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.180
Then, you get all the nutrition
of the whole food,

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:09.060
and it’s cheaper
and more stable.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:14.100
Unlike the oil, you can bake with the
seeds without destroying the omega-3s,

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:17.640
and can even store ground flaxseed
for a month, at room temperature,

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:21.605
without spoilage or oxidation.

